---
import ProductLayout from '../layouts/ProductLayout.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import FAQ from '../components/FAQ.astro';

const faqItems = [
  {
    question: 'What term lengths are typically available?',
    answer:
      'Common term lengths include 10, 15, 20, and 30 years. The right length usually lines up with a specific need, like the years remaining on a mortgage or until children are financially independent.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Does the premium change during the term?',
    answer:
      'Many term policies offer level premiums, meaning your payment stays the same for the length of the term, though this varies by product and carrier.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What happens when the term ends?',
    answer:
      'Coverage typically ends unless the policy includes a renewal or conversion option. Some term policies allow you to convert to a permanent policy without new health questions \u2014 availability depends on the product and carrier.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Is term life insurance cheaper than whole life insurance?',
    answer:
      'Term life insurance is generally more affordable than permanent coverage for the same death benefit, because it covers a limited period and doesn\u2019t build cash value. Actual pricing depends on your age, health, and the coverage amount.',
  },
];
---

<ProductLayout
  title="Term Life Insurance in Florida"
  description="Affordable, temporary life insurance coverage for a specific period \u2014 10, 15, 20, or 30 years. Compare term life insurance options in Florida."
  path="/term-life-insurance/"
  eyebrow="Florida &middot; Term Life"
  h1="Term Life Insurance in Florida"
  lead="Affordable, temporary coverage designed to protect your family for a specific period of time."
  secondaryCta={{ label: 'Compare With Whole Life', href: '/whole-life-insurance/' }}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <SectionHeading eyebrow="Overview" title="What is term life insurance?" />
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Term life insurance provides coverage for a set period of time \u2014
          typically 10, 15, 20, or 30 years. If you pass away during that
          term, your beneficiaries receive the policy's death benefit. If the
          term ends and you're still living, coverage generally stops unless
          you renew or convert the policy.
        </p>
        <p>
          Because it's designed to cover a defined period rather than your
          entire lifetime, term life insurance is typically one of the more
          affordable ways to secure a larger death benefit \u2014 which is why
          it's often used to cover specific, time-limited financial
          responsibilities.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--cloud">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <SectionHeading eyebrow="Who Considers It" title="Common reasons people choose term life" />
      <ul class="check-list" style="margin-top: var(--space-6);">
        <li>Replacing income for a spouse or family for a specific number of years</li>
        <li>Covering the remaining years on a mortgage</li>
        <li>Protecting a young family until children are financially independent</li>
        <li>Securing a larger death benefit at a more affordable premium</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <SectionHeading eyebrow="Term vs. Whole" title="Term life vs. whole life insurance" />
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          The main difference is duration and cash value. Term life covers a
          specific period and doesn't build cash value, while{' '}
          <a href="/whole-life-insurance/">whole life insurance</a> is
          permanent coverage designed to last your lifetime and may build
          cash value over time. Term is typically more affordable for the
          same death benefit; whole life typically costs more but adds a
          lifelong, cash-value component.
        </p>
        <p>
          Many people use both at different life stages \u2014 for example,
          term coverage while raising a family, and a smaller permanent
          policy for final expenses later in life. You can explore{' '}
          <a href="/final-expense-insurance/">final expense insurance</a>{' '}
          or return to the full{' '}
          <a href="/life-insurance/">overview of life insurance types</a>{' '}
          in Florida.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--cloud">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <SectionHeading eyebrow="FAQ" title="Term life insurance questions" />
      <div style="margin-top: var(--space-7);">
        <FAQ items={faqItems} />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</ProductLayout>

<style>
  .prose p {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  .prose p + p {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  .prose a {
    color: var(--color-teal-dark);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .prose a:hover {
    color: var(--color-teal);
  }
</style>
